window.NARRATION = {"ci_a": {"dur": 22.72, "text": "Pressure shows how you actually lead. This is where you start to see the gap between instinct and intention. Take about 30 seconds on each of these. Write what actually went on inside you, rather than what you think should have happened. Only you can see what you write, and it's saved here so you can come back to it. Select Save on each one as you go, then select Next.", "sents": [[0.03, "Pressure shows how you actually lead.", 0], [2.93, "This is where you start to see the gap between instinct and intention.", 0], [7.35, "Take about 30 seconds on each of these.", 1], [9.97, "Write what actually went on inside you, rather than what you think should have happened.", 1], [14.69, "Only you can see what you write, and it's saved here so you can come back to it.", 1], [19.05, "Select Save on each one as you go, then select Next.", 2]], "v": "k1", "cues": [0.03, 7.35, 19.05]}, "ci_b": {"dur": 10.8, "text": "Now look at what you wrote and pick the pattern that's closest to it. There's no right answer. Naming a habit helps you catch it sooner next time, so pick the one that best reflects your experience.", "sents": [[0.01, "Now look at what you wrote and pick the pattern that's closest to it.", 0], [3.75, "There's no right answer.", 1], [5.23, "Naming a habit helps you catch it sooner next time, so pick the one that best reflects your experience.", 1]], "v": "k1", "cues": [0.01, 3.75]}, "ci_c": {"dur": 20.08, "text": "Now run the Foundation Reset. Say your five words, the ones you saved on the Foundation Reset screen. Ask yourself for two next-best steps. Pick the one you'll take in the next ten minutes. Then take one breath and answer the anchor on the last card. It takes about a minute and works best standing up, so do it now before you move on.", "sents": [[0, "Now run the Foundation Reset.", 0], [2.15, "Say your five words, the ones you saved on the Foundation Reset screen.", 1], [6.37, "Ask yourself for two next-best steps.", 1], [9.07, "Pick the one you'll take in the next ten minutes.", 1], [11.71, "Then take one breath and answer the anchor on the last card.", 1], [15.41, "It takes about a minute and works best standing up, so do it now before you move on.", 2]], "v": "k1", "cues": [0, 2.15, 15.41]}, "kc_retry": {"dur": 3.68, "text": "Not quite. Have another look, then try again.", "sents": [[0.05, "Not quite.", 0], [1.45, "Have another look, then try again.", 0]], "v": "v4l", "cues": [0.05]}, "n_3_15": {"dur": 14.48, "text": "Time for the drill. This one tests how much certainty you need before you move. Press Play. Melissa will stop to ask what you notice, then ask you to choose, then give you a second decision. Answer each time, and the video carries on.", "sents": [[0, "Time for the drill.", 0], [1.33, "This one tests how much certainty you need before you move.", 0], [5.13, "Press Play.", 1], [6.19, "Melissa will stop to ask what you notice, then ask you to choose, then give you a second decision.", 1], [12.01, "Answer each time, and the video carries on.", 1]], "v": "v4l", "cues": [0, 5.13]}, "pc_n_3_0": {"dur": 12.8, "text": "Lesson 3 is the game plan: yours first, then your team's. You'll set one ninety-day goal for your own leadership, then learn how to bring your team to one shared goal. Select Start Lesson.", "sents": [[0.01, "Lesson 3 is the game plan: yours first, then your team's.", 0], [4.67, "You'll set one ninety-day goal for your own leadership, then learn how to bring your team to one shared goal.", 1], [11.31, "Select Start Lesson.", 1]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0.01, 4.67]}, "pc_n_3_1": {"dur": 16.0, "text": "Read this moment and picture your own team in it. Having ten priorities usually means having none. This lesson gives you one question that brings a team down to one and asks you to set your own goal first so you're modeling the focus you want from them.", "sents": [[0.07, "Read this moment and picture your own team in it.", 0], [3.79, "Having ten priorities usually means having none.", 1], [7.29, "This lesson gives you one question that brings a team down to one and asks you to set your own goal first so you're modeling the focus you want from them.", 1]], "v": "pc1", "cues": [0.07, 3.79]}, "pc_n_3_10": {"dur": 30.4, "text": "Here's the shape of the story from the video. A team had ten priorities, all urgent, but nothing was getting finished. Their manager brought them together and asked one question: “What is the one thing we must achieve this quarter to be successful?” They chose one initiative. Every weekly check-in started with it, and the team became more focused and collaborative. The question only works if you keep asking it. Your Playbook this week asks you to write your version and hold that team conversation.", "sents": [[0.03, "Here's the shape of the story from the video.", 0], [2.61, "A team had ten priorities, all urgent, but nothing was getting finished.", 1], [8.09, "Their manager brought them together and asked one question: “What is the one thing we must achieve this quarter to be successful?”", 2], [15.61, "They chose one initiative.", 3], [17.49, "Every weekly check-in started with it, and the team became more focused and collaborative.", 3], [22.59, "The question only works if you keep asking it.", 4], [25.81, "Your Playbook this week asks you to write your version and hold that team conversation.", 4]], "v": "pc1", "cues": [0.03, 2.61, 8.09, 15.61, 22.59]}, "pc_n_3_12": {"dur": 28.48, "text": "Here's the sequence from the budget-cut story, step by step. First, name the new reality out loud. It tells the team you're not pretending the problem away. Then ask what's still possible. The goal stays alive, but now you must work within the constraint. Ask what the constraint forces you to consider. That's where the creative options come from. Then stop talking. The team's answer is the one they'll own, and next time, they'll start there without you.", "sents": [[0.01, "Here's the sequence from the budget-cut story, step by step.", 0], [3.91, "First, name the new reality out loud.", 1], [7.11, "It tells the team you're not pretending the problem away.", 1], [10.33, "Then ask what's still possible.", 2], [12.77, "The goal stays alive, but now you must work within the constraint.", 2], [16.91, "Ask what the constraint forces you to consider.", 3], [19.65, "That's where the creative options come from.", 3], [21.95, "Then stop talking.", 4], [23.81, "The team's answer is the one they'll own, and next time, they'll start there without you.", 4]], "v": "pc1", "cues": [0.01, 3.91, 10.33, 16.91, 21.95]}, "pc_n_3_13": {"dur": 9.44, "text": "Let's test it in the moment it's hardest. Your team's plan just lost its budget, and they're looking at you. Pick your first sentence, and you'll hear where it leads.", "sents": [[0, "Let's test it in the moment it's hardest.", 0], [2.89, "Your team's plan just lost its budget, and they're looking at you.", 1], [6.75, "Pick your first sentence, and you'll hear where it leads.", 1]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0, 2.89]}, "pc_n_3_13_o0": {"dur": 11.2, "text": "It's quick and it sounds decisive. It also takes the problem away from the people who need to learn to solve it, so at the next roadblock they'll wait for you again. Try the other option to compare.", "sents": [[0, "It's quick and it sounds decisive.", 0], [2.91, "It also takes the problem away from the people who need to learn to solve it, so at the next roadblock they'll wait for you again.", 0], [9.55, "Try the other option to compare.", 0]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0]}, "pc_n_3_13_o1": {"dur": 8.64, "text": "You named the reality, kept the goal alive and handed the thinking back to the team with the constraint attached. That's coaching through a roadblock.", "sents": [[0.01, "You named the reality, kept the goal alive and handed the thinking back to the team with the constraint attached.", 0], [6.71, "That's coaching through a roadblock.", 0]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0.01]}, "pc_n_3_15": {"dur": 36.48, "text": "Your core rep this week is your own game plan, which takes about twenty minutes: one leadership goal, the roadblock most likely to derail it, and the Core 4 pillar it will test. Add it to your Scorecard as well. If you have more time, write your version of the one-goal question, hold the team conversation, and record the shared goal and how often you'll review progress toward it. Also, write the two questions you'll ask when the first roadblock hits. Then share your goal with your Athleader in this week's check-in and ask about the purpose they're defining. Select Open your Lesson 3 pages to get started.", "sents": [[0.01, "Your core rep this week is your own game plan, which takes about twenty minutes: one leadership goal, the roadblock most likely to derail it, and the Core 4 pillar it will test.", 0], [11.25, "Add it to your Scorecard as well.", 0], [13.25, "If you have more time, write your version of the one-goal question, hold the team conversation, and record the shared goal and how often you'll review progress toward it.", 1], [22.95, "Also, write the two questions you'll ask when the first roadblock hits.", 2], [27.37, "Then share your goal with your Athleader in this week's check-in and ask about the purpose they're defining.", 3], [33.21, "Select Open your Lesson 3 pages to get started.", 3]], "v": "pc1", "cues": [0.01, 13.25, 22.95, 27.37]}, "pc_n_3_16": {"dur": 12.4, "text": "This lesson's Athleader Pro is Stephanie Johnson, the Momentum Maker. She leads her own company and talks about turning adversity into momentum for both a team and yourself. Press Play to hear from her.", "sents": [[0, "This lesson's Athleader Pro is Stephanie Johnson, the Momentum Maker.", 0], [4.87, "She leads her own company and talks about turning adversity into momentum for both a team and yourself.", 1], [11.11, "Press Play to hear from her.", 1]], "v": "pc1", "cues": [0, 4.87]}, "pc_n_3_17": {"dur": 12.72, "text": "Stephanie's drill helps you realign under pressure and takes three minutes. Select Start the timer and work through each step. When you've completed the drill or scheduled a time to run it, select the option that fits.", "sents": [[0.05, "Stephanie's drill helps you realign under pressure and takes three minutes.", 0], [4.77, "Select Start the timer and work through each step.", 1], [8.01, "When you've completed the drill or scheduled a time to run it, select the option that fits.", 1]], "v": "pc1", "cues": [0.05, 4.77]}, "pc_n_3_19_q0": {"dur": 7.6, "text": "A few questions on the main ideas. First: which of these is a ninety-day leadership goal rather than a project goal?", "sents": [[0, "A few questions on the main ideas.", 0], [2.31, "First: which of these is a ninety-day leadership goal rather than a project goal?", 0]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0]}, "pc_n_3_19_q1": {"dur": 4.16, "text": "Why do you set your own ninety-day goal before your team sets theirs?", "sents": [[0.05, "Why do you set your own ninety-day goal before your team sets theirs?", 0]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0.05]}, "pc_n_3_19_q2": {"dur": 4.88, "text": "Your team chose its one shared goal. What keeps it alive through the quarter?", "sents": [[0.01, "Your team chose its one shared goal.", 0], [3.01, "What keeps it alive through the quarter?", 0]], "v": "r3", "cues": [0.01]}, "pc_n_3_19_q3": {"dur": 5.28, "text": "Last one. The first roadblock hits. What is your role as a Player-Coach?", "sents": [[0.01, "Last one.", 0], [1.09, "The first roadblock hits.", 0], [3.21, "What is your role as a Player-Coach?", 0]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0.01]}, "pc_n_3_19_w0": {"dur": 8.16, "text": "It changes how you spend your time as a leader, and it has a clear start date. The others are outputs the team delivers.", "sents": [[0, "It changes how you spend your time as a leader, and it has a clear start date.", 0], [5.51, "The others are outputs the team delivers.", 0]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0]}, "pc_n_3_19_w1": {"dur": 9.2, "text": "A team takes focus from what its leader does. Having your own plan also shows you where the roadblocks are before you ask anyone else to face them.", "sents": [[0.07, "A team takes focus from what its leader does.", 0], [3.29, "Having your own plan also shows you where the roadblocks are before you ask anyone else to face them.", 0]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0.07]}, "pc_n_3_19_w2": {"dur": 8.88, "text": "The question only works if you keep asking it. Opening every weekly check-in with the shared goal keeps the team on one priority instead of ten.", "sents": [[0, "The question only works if you keep asking it.", 0], [3.29, "Opening every weekly check-in with the shared goal keeps the team on one priority instead of ten.", 0]], "v": "r3", "cues": [0]}, "pc_n_3_19_w3": {"dur": 9.92, "text": "If you clear every roadblock, the team learns to wait for you. Naming the reality and asking what's still possible builds their ability to solve the next one.", "sents": [[0, "If you clear every roadblock, the team learns to wait for you.", 0], [4.33, "Naming the reality and asking what's still possible builds their ability to solve the next one.", 0]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0]}, "pc_n_3_20": {"dur": 32.24, "text": "Before you go, here's what to keep from this lesson. Your own ninety-day goal comes first. You're modeling the focus you want to see. One question brings a team from ten priorities to one: “What is the one thing we must achieve this quarter?” Then you ask it again every week. And when the roadblock comes, name the reality, ask what's still possible, and let the team find the way. Select Download my answers for a Word document containing what you wrote today. Chapter 11 of the book is all about the 90-Day Way.", "sents": [[0.05, "Before you go, here's what to keep from this lesson.", 0], [3.37, "Your own ninety-day goal comes first.", 1], [6.23, "You're modeling the focus you want to see.", 1], [8.91, "One question brings a team from ten priorities to one: “What is the one thing we must achieve this quarter?”", 2], [15.83, "Then you ask it again every week.", 2], [17.03, "And when the roadblock comes, name the reality, ask what's still possible, and let the team find the way.", 3], [24.59, "Select Download my answers for a Word document containing what you wrote today.", 4], [28.95, "Chapter 11 of the book is all about the 90-Day Way.", 4]], "v": "pc1", "cues": [0.05, 3.37, 8.91, 17.03, 24.59]}, "pc_n_3_21": {"dur": 19.92, "text": "That's Lesson 3 done. You're halfway through your season, and your team can see it. This week, run your core rep: write your ninety-day leadership goal. Then share it with your Athleader during your check-in and ask about the purpose they're working on. Next time, you'll explore pressure and what your team learns from how you handle it.", "sents": [[0.05, "That's Lesson 3 done.", 0], [1.83, "You're halfway through your season, and your team can see it.", 0], [5.77, "This week, run your core rep: write your ninety-day leadership goal.", 1], [7.97, "Then share it with your Athleader during your check-in and ask about the purpose they're working on.", 1], [15.39, "Next time, you'll explore pressure and what your team learns from how you handle it.", 1]], "v": "pc1", "cues": [0.05, 5.77]}, "pc_n_3_3": {"dur": 6.16, "text": "A quick look back at Lesson 2 before you start. Choose the answer you remember. This one isn't scored.", "sents": [[0, "A quick look back at Lesson 2 before you start.", 0], [2.91, "Choose the answer you remember.", 1], [4.69, "This one isn't scored.", 1]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0, 2.91]}, "pc_n_3_4": {"dur": 32.64, "text": "Here's what you'll practice in this lesson. You'll write one ninety-day goal about how you lead: something specific and measurable, with a start date, that focuses on your leadership rather than a project. You'll name the one habit or meeting most likely to derail your goal and which of the Core 4 it will test. You'll learn the question that brings a team from ten priorities to one and how to keep it in front of the team every week. And when the first roadblock arrives, you'll have a way to coach the team through it instead of removing the roadblock yourself.", "sents": [[0.01, "Here's what you'll practice in this lesson.", 0], [2.37, "You'll write one ninety-day goal about how you lead: something specific and measurable, with a start date, that focuses on your leadership rather than a project.", 1], [11.87, "You'll name the one habit or meeting most likely to derail your goal and which of the Core 4 it will test.", 2], [19.03, "You'll learn the question that brings a team from ten priorities to one and how to keep it in front of the team every week.", 3], [24.93, "And when the first roadblock arrives, you'll have a way to coach the team through it instead of removing the roadblock yourself.", 4]], "v": "pc1", "cues": [0.01, 2.37, 11.87, 19.03, 24.93]}, "pc_n_3_7": {"dur": 27.52, "text": "The 90-Day Way works at two levels, and yours comes first. Your own goal is about how you lead. Melissa's example is that of a manager who delegated one significant responsibility to free up five hours a week for strategic thinking. It's specific and measurable, and it changes how she works. Then you bring the same system to your team. One question gets them to one shared goal, and every weekly check-in opens with it.", "sents": [[0.03, "The 90-Day Way works at two levels, and yours comes first.", 0], [4.47, "Your own goal is about how you lead.", 1], [7.39, "Melissa's example is that of a manager who delegated one significant responsibility to free up five hours a week for strategic thinking.", 1], [15.59, "It's specific and measurable, and it changes how she works.", 1], [19.69, "Then you bring the same system to your team.", 2], [22.59, "One question gets them to one shared goal, and every weekly check-in opens with it.", 2]], "v": "pc1", "cues": [0.03, 4.47, 19.69]}, "pc_n_3_8": {"dur": 13.6, "text": "Try this before you write your own. For each goal, decide whether it's about your leadership or about a project. The test is simple. A leadership goal changes something about how you lead, and you could start it next week.", "sents": [[0.03, "Try this before you write your own.", 0], [2.25, "For each goal, decide whether it's about your leadership or about a project.", 0], [7.09, "The test is simple.", 1], [8.63, "A leadership goal changes something about how you lead, and you could start it next week.", 1]], "v": "r3L", "cues": [0.03, 7.09]}, "r2_code_pulse": {"dur": 7.36, "text": "Type the code from the last page of the Pulse Check, then select Submit. A quick knowledge check comes next, then your recap.", "sents": [[0.01, "Type the code from the last page of the Pulse Check, then select Submit.", 0], [4.23, "A quick knowledge check comes next, then your recap.", 0]], "v": "r3", "cues": [0.01]}, "r2_form_pulse": {"dur": 8.96, "text": "Answer the five questions, then select Submit. Your code appears on the last page. Copy the code or write it down, then select Next.", "sents": [[0, "Answer the five questions, then select Submit.", 0], [3.25, "Your code appears on the last page.", 0], [5.45, "Copy the code or write it down, then select Next.", 0]], "v": "r3", "cues": [0]}, "r2_pulse": {"dur": 21.36, "text": "Every lesson has the same short Pulse Check, a check-in that helps you see how you're changing over the season. It asks how often you've practiced each of the Core 4 and completed your reps in the last two weeks. It takes about a minute, and your answers go to the Athleadership team, who use them to see how the whole group is progressing. Select Next, and it opens right here.", "sents": [[0.01, "Every lesson has the same short Pulse Check, a check-in that helps you see how you're changing over the season.", 0], [6.57, "It asks how often you've practiced each of the Core 4 and completed your reps in the last two weeks.", 1], [12.25, "It takes about a minute, and your answers go to the Athleadership team, who use them to see how the whole group is progressing.", 2], [18.83, "Select Next, and it opens right here.", 2]], "v": "k1", "cues": [0.01, 6.57, 12.25]}};
